' Usage Examples
note as UsageExample
    **Usage Example:**

    // Create and configure MQ adapter
    parallel_mq_adapter* mq = create_rabbitmq_adapter();
    struct parallel_mq_config config = {
        .base = {.type = ADAPTER_TYPE_MQ, .name = "task_queue"},
        .host = "localhost", .port = 5672
    };
    mq->configure(mq, &config);
    mq->connect(mq);

    // Send message
    struct parallel_mq_message msg = {
        .routing_key = "tasks",
        .body = "process_data",
        .priority = MSG_PRIORITY_NORMAL
    };
    mq->publish(mq, &msg);
end note

' Design Patterns Used
note as DesignPatterns
    **Design Patterns Applied:**

    **Adapter Pattern:**
    - Unified interface for different protocols
    - Pluggable implementations

    **Factory Pattern:**
    - Registry-based adapter creation
    - Type-safe instantiation

    **Observer Pattern:**
    - Async callbacks for responses
    - Event-driven notifications

    **Strategy Pattern:**
    - Configurable retry/error handling
    - Pluggable authentication methods

    **Template Method:**
    - Standardized lifecycle (configure→connect→execute→disconnect)
    - Consistent error handling
end note

' Benefits
note as Benefits
    **Framework Benefits:**

    **Consistency:**
    - Unified configuration and lifecycle
    - Consistent error handling across protocols

    **Extensibility:**
    - Easy addition of new adapters
    - Protocol-agnostic application code

    **Reliability:**
    - Built-in retry and timeout mechanisms
    - Health monitoring and metrics

    **Maintainability:**
    - Clear separation of concerns
    - Testable adapter implementations
end note

@enduml
